<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
<title>CLASKNN: Classification by number of nearest neighbors</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>
<body>
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->


<p align="justify">This module allows doing a supervised classification based on the k nearest neighboring of training areas in the statistical space.</p> 
<p align="justify">For each pixel of the image to classify, the Euclidean distance is calculated with each pixel of the training areas on the space representation of the origin bands. The k nearest training areas pixels is chosen and the predominant class of this group of pixels is the class that is assigned to the pixel to be classified. To calculate the dominant class, two options are allowed: the first by mode and the second applying a weight according to the inverse of the distance. The input file must be an IMG raster format and data type can be any of those supported by MiraMon (<a href="..%5Cmm32%5CAP1.htm">Consult raster formats supported by MiraMon</a>).</p>
 <p>The pixels that have a NODATA value in some of the bands or variables can
  be classified using the MaxBandsNODATA parameter, which indicates the
  maximum number of variables with a NODATA value that are tolerated in order
  not to mark the pixel as unclassified. This parameter may oscillate between
  0 and n_bands-1:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>0: Only if a variable is NODATA, the pixel is considered not classified.</li>

    <li>n_bands-1: this is the most tolerant situation, in which the pixel is
    classified with only one different NODATA value in any of the bands. To
    define this value, it is necessary write MAX in the parameter and the
    program will calculate it according to the bands used.</li>
  </ul>


<p align="justify">In contrast to other classifiers, in which the number of samples used to define classes is not relevant in the allocation phase, the kNN is significantly slower when more samples exist.</p>

<p align="justify">In order to interpret the distance values used by this classifier, we recommend reading the "Guidance on the meaning of the distances used in the classification processes" in the help of the ClasSup module.</p> 

